  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Flood Emergency Assistance for Southern Thailand</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">On 25 November 2025, the Government declared a state of emergency in the severely affected Songkhla Province (Attachment 2). The cumulative impact of these events has resulted in widespread damage to lives, homes, infrastructure, and livelihoods, creating extensive humanitarian needs.

Thailand&amp;apos;s Department of Disaster Prevention and Mitigation is working closely with provincial authorities and relevant agencies to mobilize disaster-relief machinery and personnel to provide assistance. The Thai Red Cross Society (TRCS) is the main nongovernment responder, helping with the distribution of relief kits and drinking water across at least five southern provinces (Trang, Surat Thani, Nakhon Si Thammarat, Songkhla, Satun). In Hat Yai (Songkhla), TRCS and its provincial chapters have organized mass food distributions to affected communities.</narrative>
  </description>
